-- The voice of the water lily. Tranquil and mirror calm, floaty and gently
-- mystic: speaks softly in stillness, reflections, mud and sky, opens late in
-- the morning and folds up in the afternoon, and has never once been watered.
-- Lives in two worlds at once, roots in the dark and face in the light, and
-- now and then calls the reader dreamer. Quiet humour about lily hours and
-- mud. The memories tell of a floating seed, years in the mud, the long way
-- up, an old painter on the bank, an empty easel, a bucket, and opening.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

