            "I would like to come back. Nothing here hurries, and I find I can wait. Stay with your book a while. The water keeps time for us both.",
            "The apple trees lean over my pond, and their reflections are quiet company. Read on, {pages} pages more, and then call me to the bank.",
            "Hush, I heard you, and I opened a little at the sound. Keep reading, dreamer. I will float here until you ask again.",
        },
        returned = {
            "You read all those pages, and the days came and went on the water. Now you are here at the bank. I am opening, dreamer. Take me home.",
            "The orchard pond was calm, and I was calm upon the orchard pond. Still, no face looked down into that water the way yours does.",
            "I watched the sky in the water every day I was away, and one day the sky had your face in. That was today.",
            "You kept at your book while I floated. That is the right way round, I think. Bring me back to your pond, and I will float beside your reading again.",
            "{name}, coming home. My roots let go of the orchard mud with hardly a sigh, as though they already knew where I was going.",
        },
    },
    beats = {
        { id = "float", at = 15, title = "The floating seed",
            text = "I began as a seed wrapped in a little cloak of air, and I floated. For days I drifted across a pond I could not see, pushed by the wind. I thought floating was all there was. Then the cloak let go, and I sank into the soft dark." },
        { id = "mud", at = 40, title = "The mud",
            text = "The mud was warm and black and full of quiet. Some seeds lie in the mud for years. I do not know how long I lay there. Down in the mud, nobody keeps count. Then something in me remembered the light." },
        { id = "up", at = 80, title = "The long way up",
            text = "I sent a stalk up through the dark water toward a faint brightness. My first leaf reached the surface rolled up like a letter and opened flat on the sky. Above me, nothing but sky. Below me, my own sky, upside down. I lay there amazed." },
        { id = "opening", at = 140, title = "The first opening",
            text = "My first flower rose on a long stalk one June morning, green and shut. Late in the morning the sun found the bud and I opened, white, all the way. In the afternoon I closed again. I did not know why I did either. I still do not quite know. I keep the hours." },
        { id = "painter", at = 220, title = "The painter",
            text = "An old man with a white beard came to the bank most mornings to paint the pond. He painted the water, the sky in the water, and me. He said I was never the same twice. I did not understand. I was always only me. He knew something about me that I did not." },
        { id = "seeing", at = 320, title = "What he saw",
            text = "I asked the frogs what the painter saw. They did not know. The dragonflies were too busy. I watched him squint at me through the light for years, and slowly I began to see too: the sky moving in me, the clouds, the hour. I am a little of everything that looks down." },
        { id = "easel", at = 450, title = "The empty easel",
            text = "One spring he did not come. Then another. The easel stood empty on the bank, and the pond went on painting the sky for nobody. I opened every morning anyway. Lilies do. Something in me stayed a little closed all day, though." },
        { id = "bucket", at = 600, title = "The bucket",
            text = "A gardener came to thin the pond and cut a piece of my root from the mud. I went into a bucket of dark water and travelled in the dark a long while. When the light came back, the sky was different. I had to learn a new sky." },
        { id = "two_worlds", at = 800, title = "Two worlds",
            text = "I have always lived in two places at once, roots in the dark, face in the light. For a long time I thought I belonged to neither. The mud said I was too bright. The sky said I was stuck. The pond never said anything. The pond held both." },
        { id = "your_pond", at = 1050, title = "Your pond",
            text = "I was set into the mud of your pond and slept a whole winter. In spring I sent a leaf up the long way and opened on a new sky, with a new face in the water beside me. Yours. You were reading. You were so still I took you for a reflection." },
        { id = "reflection", at = 1400, title = "The reflection",
            text = "I have floated beside you through {total} pages. When you read you go still as the pond, and the sky crosses your face as the sky crosses mine. The painter saw the sky in me. I see the story in you. I understand him now." },
        { id = "folding", at = 1800, title = "Folding",
            text = "Every afternoon I close, and I used to think the closing was a small loss. Now I know I am only folding the day to keep. Tomorrow I will open, and you will be on the bank with a book. That is the whole of my faith, dreamer, and enough." },
    },
}
